  prose(<<~'CANONICAL_PROSE', origin: :published)
    ## Overview
    
    The Aerie Perch is a crystal-spired trade post on The Berg's eastern reach, comprising seven aurora-crystal spires raised during the Frozen Peace by Qingqe'frostling settlers affiliated with Qingfu'spire, the Aurora Stack surface faction. It was the first permanent structure the Qingqe'frostlings built — a fact worth noting, since what a settlement raises first reveals what it values most. They built a trade post, not a temple.
    
    The spires once caught aurora-light in synchronized spirals. They no longer do. Several now tilt at angles that scatter light unevenly, and three or four are dark at any given time. The main gallery ceiling, carved from a single aurora-crystal block, is webbed with cracks. The structure functions. It does not thrive.
    
    ## Political Fracture
    
    The Perch's current condition is inseparable from the schism that split Qingfu'spire. Plunge-Caller Oeichowei, the Storm-Caller — a mystic who emerged from the Promenade Ward's collapse to lead the splinter faction known as The Pinnacle — seized the upper galleries following her break with the parent council. The Pinnacle now occupies the Perch alongside Qingfu'spire loyalists, neither faction willing to cede the structure entirely.
    
    Locals call the site "the Contested Spire," though never within earshot of whoever holds authority that week. The older name — *The Watching* — persists among residents, who decline to explain its origin. The floor of the main gallery still bears deliberate gouges from the merchant-guard seizure three winters past, and someone carved "Oeichowei was here first" into the support-ice near the north entrance. The scorch marks remain. No one has smoothed them.
    
    ## Trade Function
    
    The Perch continues to operate as an exchange point under the Flipper Accord. Nightshelf merchants ascend the eastern approach twice per season to trade volcanic stone and fire-cores for aurora-crystals, their flippers cloth-wrapped against the surface cold. The third-tier gallery — originally ceremonial — now serves as crystal storage, with crates sorted by luminosity. Food stalls along the gallery's edge supply preserved fish and kelp tea.
    
    The sub-audible hum in the ice underfoot comes from Pinnacle practitioners working the Mechanism Refine technique in the upper spires — a process of channeling aurora-light to repair fractured fire-cores, documented in the chronicle accounts of the crystal-worker known as Cold-flip Qing. The main gallery still carries the residual scent of rendered fire-core and the iron trace of trade-rite blood.
    
    Trade persists here because the Accord demands it, and because neither faction can afford to let it fail.
    
    ## The Deep Vault
    
    Below the trade galleries, The Pinnacle maintains a vault containing the Radiant Aurora-harp, seized from Aurora Stack's council chamber during the succession crisis following the death of Veil☽ Glow, an elder mystic. The harp bears three fracture lines — two from earlier conflicts, one from Ice-Crowned Shexuwohua's seizure during the crisis itself. Stored light catches along the fractures and throws shadows that move without apparent source. The Pinnacle has not returned the instrument. Qingfu'spire has not stopped demanding it.
