  annotation "note_1771590427566_0", anchor: "webbed with cracks. The structure functions. It does not thrive.", text: "The main text attributes the damage to neglect and factional decay. It does not mention the Grulkzul Omega Strike. The deep-ice impression at stratum 4-east preserves a pressure-event radiating from the gallery floor — the signature of ice split from within, not weathered from without. Orca coven blood-workings leave residue patterns distinct from structural settling: radial fractures, not gravitational ones. The ceiling cracks are radial. I wrote this entry as though the Perch is dying of politics. The ice says something hit it. I could not determine when, and I was not willing to guess in the main text, so I let the cracks speak for themselves. They deserve better than my silence.", type: :correction, display: :full
  annotation "note_1771590427566_1", anchor: "They built a trade post, not a temple.", text: "They built for exchange. For the expectation of someone arriving.", type: :commentary, display: :popout
  annotation "note_1771590427566_2", anchor: "The older name — *The Watching* — persists among residents, who decline to explain its origin.", text: "Eastern reach. Open sightlines to the frozen sea. The name predates the schism, predates the Pinnacle, predates Oeichowei. Residents decline to explain — not cannot, decline. The Berg's eastern face is where the Long Dark arrives first and lifts last. What one watches for from a perch on the eastern edge, during four months of darkness, with the veil at its thinnest — I will not speculate in a margin note. But the name was given before anyone had a faction to watch.", type: :commentary, display: :full
